
What's new in version 2.0.0
---------------------------

- Drop support for Python 2.
  * Drop [PyAMF](https://pypi.org/project/PyAMF/) dependency.
  * Drop [HessianPy](https://pypi.org/project/HessianPy/) dependency.

- Components tested with Trac>=0.12, TracXmlRPC>=1.2.0 and Python>=3.13.13.

- Support for AMF protocol implemented by [Py3AMF](https://github.com/StdCarrot/Py3AMF) library.

- Support for Hessian serialization implemented by [python-hessian](https://github.com/theatlantic/python-hessian) library.

- Hessian RPC no longer available at /hessian.

- Hessian available at /rpc when content type application/x-hessian is requested.

- AMF RPC no longer available at /amf.

- AMF RPC available at /rpc when content type application/x-amf is requested

- Log RPC errors at custom level between ERROR and WARNING.

- On error, return log ref ID to the caller instead of full stack traces.

- Tests for Hessian protocol implementation using
  [python-hessian](https://github.com/theatlantic/python-hessian) client.

What's new in version 1.0.0
---------------------------

- Support for Hessian RPC.

- Support for Adobe's Action Message Format (thanks to 
  `thijs <http://trac-hacks.org/wiki/thijs>`_ for the original patch).
